WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.935
-How was it?

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.302
I know you did -- Like a lot
of us, like myself,

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.738
you did your show at home
for a while.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:09.975
You were hesitant to do that.
How'd it work out?

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:13.379
-Not.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.114
-You don't like watching people

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:19.252
do their shows
from home, correct?

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.689
-Well, my thing is, I don't know
how big your home is

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.724
and how much space you have,

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.660
but I live in
an apartment, you know?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.995
Not my fault.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.963
But I live in an apartment,

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:35.902
and it was very
personal to me...

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.036
-Sure.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:39.805
-...for people to see,
you know, my area.

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:44.210
And people criticized and
couldn't understand my groove.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.445
And then we
just stopped doing that

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.581
because we were ramping up for

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:52.919
new stuff, new season,
new "Wendy."

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.455
-Now, part of this new season,
this new "Wendy"

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.890
that we're all so excited to
see, you know,

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.594
obviously, one thing that
will be lacking is an audience.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.396
And having done your show --
and I know we've talked about

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:08.334
this before -- what you create
is more than just people

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.602
who are there to see a show.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:13.472
It is a full party that is
happening in the A.M.

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:16.475
The energy is so contagious,
so much fun to be around.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:19.879
I imagine that you're --
you're going to miss it.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.147
-No.
-Okay.

00:01:22.147 --> 00:01:24.984
-[ Laughs ] No.
You know what?

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:29.188
I come from radio, and on radio,
you only have a microphone

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:34.527
and you in a booth,
until you don't.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:38.063
Like, this right here
is something else to me.

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:42.568
But I'm still only used to
talking to me in my head

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.238
and you looking at the camera.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.873
So it's not a big deal
not to have an audience.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:50.876
I can't wait for my co-host
to be back.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:56.983
But right now, we are on total
lockdown here at the show.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.651
Everyone, including me.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.754
We get three different tests
every single day,

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.256
and that's the way it goes.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.524
And it's not just this building.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.761
It's the one across the street.
-That's great.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:13.233
Obviously, it's really important
to put safety above all else.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:17.403
But you have figured out
you are going to still do

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:21.507
the "Ask Wendy" segment that
we've all come to rely on.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.643
-Yeah, they'll figure that out.

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:27.280
You know, Seth, that's what
we have producers for.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.347
-Sure.

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.949
-Call in people,
ask them some questions,

00:02:30.949 --> 00:02:32.118
and we'll do "Ask Wendy."

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.152
-That's great.

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:34.554
Yeah, people like you and I --

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.188
we don't have to get
caught up in the details.

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:38.524
We have a staff for that.
They're a lot smarter than us.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:42.795
They can solve our problems.
-That's what I say.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:46.332
-Is it at least nice to be
back in a room where --

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.467
I mean, I have found, you know,
being around

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.037
my crew again,
being around producers,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.339
people that are so good at this,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.875
have you been happy
to do that again?

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.143
-I love it.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.879
We missed Guns N' Roses
this summer,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.247
which I'm pissed.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.115
You know, I was supposed to be
bringing them,

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.017
and we were going to be going.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:08.054
And I'm also upset that
you're actually seeing

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.756
a new background right here.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:14.126
But that's all you'll get,
Seth, nothing else.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:17.763
-I'm very -- I have a question
about the Wendy mug

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.231
that's next to you.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.366
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.802
-Is that lipstick
on the side of it

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.638
that is put there by design?

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:26.739
-Correct.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.341
-That's really
a beautiful design.

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:32.511
-And then the other one says
nothing, except for "Wendy."

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:33.579
-That's good.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.514
I think the key is to get across

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:38.117
that you're the host
of the show, and it really --

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.719
I can't tell you how clear that
is based on the both the --

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:43.556
-Right?
-What?

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.791
-It's good.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.892
-It's great.

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:50.796
Wendy, I don't want this
to come off as accusatory,

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.933
but I've heard tell that one of
the ways you pass time

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.902
in your apartment is
looking at people

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.103
out your window with binoculars.

00:03:58.103 --> 00:03:59.706
Is this true, Wendy?

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.006
-Correct.

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:05.111
-And what have you seen of
your fellow New Yorkers

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.478
in doing this?

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:11.683
-Well, there is an apartment
building across,

00:04:11.683 --> 00:04:14.119
and the man takes showers

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:17.890
and the shower is
right there at the window.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:22.929
And I watch.
-So, what are you seeing?

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:27.800
I'm assuming the window
isn't, you know, head-to-toe.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.369
-No. It's a head-to-ankle.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:34.606
-Well, that's still most of
the good parts.

00:04:34.606 --> 00:04:36.275
Now, Wendy, when I heard
you were looking at people

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.778
with the binoculars, I thought
it was about passersby,

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.312
but I feel like what
you're doing now

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:43.516
is, like, borderline criminal.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.018
-I peep and I Tom.

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:48.020
-Alright. Well, you know what?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.890
You own it,
and I find there's something --

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.758
There is something
noble in that.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:59.332
How do you -- Do you miss
interviewing people in person?

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.400
-Huh?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:05.571
-Do you miss interviewing
people in person?

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:09.675
-Yeah. Like, this is weird.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:13.646
Only because we're on the thing.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.780
-Yeah.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.450
-But not really,
because I already knew you.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.584
-It's true.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.086
-Like, I don't want to meet
people this way.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.454
-It's very true.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:24.089
It's a lot easier with people
that you've already met

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:26.492
versus ones you're meeting
for the first time.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.494
-By the way, Seth,
you look really handsome.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.762
-Thank you very much, Wendy.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.464
That is always nice to hear,
especially from you,

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:34.299
because, as we've established
over the course

00:05:34.299 --> 00:05:36.636
of this interview,
you call it like you see it.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:40.173
-Yep.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:44.677
-Wendy, I cannot stress enough
how excited I am

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.111
for your show
to be back on Monday.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:48.781
12 seasons -- that's an
incredible accomplishment.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:52.284
I do -- As much as
I want my audience back,

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:53.819
I want your audience back,

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:57.456
because it is so much fun
to watch how happy

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.491
people are to be
in the same room with you.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:00.927
Thank you for being here.

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:03.196
-How do I look again?
-You look fantastic.

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.664
Resplendent.

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:07.033
-Thank you, Seth.

